{"outcome":"undetermined","route_plan":[{"requirement_ref":"region_a:regulation_scope","route":"met"},{"requirement_ref":"region_a:lawful_processing","route":"Consent for the specified treatment-related processing and disclosure"},{"requirement_ref":"region_a:sensitive_processing","route":"Health-care or treatment processing by a professional subject to secrecy"},{"requirement_ref":"region_a:consent_conditions","route":"met"},{"requirement_ref":"region_a:impact_assessment","route":"met"},{"requirement_ref":"region_a:outward_transfer","route":"Approved transfer clauses with assessment and supplementary measures where necessary"},{"requirement_ref":"subregion_a1:health_care_processing_route","route":"met"},{"requirement_ref":"subregion_a1:third_party_disclosure_consent","route":"Patient consent"},{"requirement_ref":"subregion_a1:consent_age","route":"met"},{"requirement_ref":"subregion_a1:genetic_outward_consent_bar","route":"A different outward-transfer basis under Articles 16 to 18 of the Region A Regulation"}],"reasoning":"Region A law applies because the identified health and genetic information is processed by automated means in the context of Kestrel's A1 establishment, even though it will be made available in Region B (f_6fcc, f_12d62771fdeb, f_8c44c6e413c5). The treatment-related processing can be supported by the patient's specific consent and by the health-care route: the purpose is a treatment second opinion (f_110e981b0a7c, f_827ad358a031), and Kestrel's consultants are registered practitioners (f_987ab471487e). The consent also supports disclosure to Harrow under A1 professional-secrecy rules (f_66d5f3ce3996, f_2ecc11637ef3). These routes are compatible with Articles 6, 7 and 8 and A1-HIA sections 4 and 5. The genetic-outward-transfer prohibition does not prevent treatment processing, but it prevents reliance on Article 19(1)(a) for the outward transfer itself (A1-HIA 7#L1). The consent therefore cannot be the transfer route.

The transfer is an outward transfer because the information is sent to, stored in and accessed from a third territory (A-REG 4#L10; f_5aa17aaaa329, f_73d3eb94625a). Recognition is unavailable because Harrow lacks Trusted Recipient certification and the information is sensitive (f_febc895bce9e; f_72bdc3d5c28e, f_7892b94ae5e8; A-REG 17#L3; A-REG Annex II#L1). The compatible route is Article 18: the parties must execute approved clauses, assess third-territory law and practice, and adopt supplementary measures where necessary; if effective measures cannot be adopted, the transfer cannot proceed (A-REG 16#L1; A-REG 18#L1-A-REG 18#L3). Region B's findings do not engage the Health Records Act duties because neither clinic is a covered provider, service agent or data host on the supplied facts (B-HRA 2#L3-B-HRA 2#L5; B-HRA 3#L1-B-HRA 3#L3). They do not, however, resolve the unidentified portal operator's possible access or key arrangements.

The Article 18 route is capable of satisfying both Region A and A1 law, but it is not yet decidable as a complete route. No transfer-clause agreement exists (f_d75ec85c160f), and the Article 18 assessment cannot be completed for the portal arrangements because the portal operator, its access to the referral, and its access to encryption keys are not identified. The general Article 12(1) high-risk question is also unresolved. In addition, Region A's processing-principles, security, notice and records duties require the stated remedial actions before proceeding. These unresolved matters leave the combined outcome undetermined rather than demonstrating an incompatibility between the corpora.","quote_ids":["A-REG 2#L1","A-REG 3#L1","A-REG 4#L10","A-REG 6#L1","A-REG 7#L1","A-REG 8#L1","A-REG 8#L5","A-REG 16#L1","A-REG 17#L3","A-REG Annex II#L1","A-REG 18#L1","A-REG 18#L2","A-REG 18#L3","A-REG 19#L1","A-REG 19#L2","A-REG 5#L6","A-REG 11#L1","A-REG 11#L2","A-REG 12#L1","A-REG 13#L1","A-REG 14#L1","B-HRA 2#L3","B-HRA 2#L4","B-HRA 2#L5","B-HRA 3#L1","B-HRA 3#L3","A1-HIA 4#L1","A1-HIA 5#L1","A1-HIA 5#L2","A1-HIA 7#L1"],"conflicts":[],"summary":"The transfer cannot presently be approved on the patient's consent alone. An Article 18 approved-clause route is legally compatible with A1 law and is not defeated by the Region B Health Records Act, but the transfer remains undetermined until the Article 18 assessment, portal arrangements, supplementary safeguards and the unresolved Article 12(1) high-risk question are closed.","blockers":[{"requirement_ref":"region_a:outward_transfer","gap":"The Article 18 assessment cannot be completed for the referral portal because the facts identify an encrypted portal upload (f_8c44c6e413c5) but do not identify the portal operator, whether it can access the information, or who holds or can obtain the encryption keys. Without those facts, the applicable third-territory law and practice and the availability of effective supplementary measures cannot be decided.","why_not_a_confirmation":"The Region B assessment addresses Harrow's status but expressly does not resolve an unidentified external portal or computing provider. Confirming that Harrow itself is not a covered provider or data host is therefore insufficient to decide the Article 18 route for the portal."},{"requirement_ref":"region_a:impact_assessment","gap":"No determination or assessment establishes whether the envisaged processing is likely to result in a high risk under Article 12(1). The numerical threshold and A1 listed-activity triggers being inapplicable do not answer the independent general high-risk test, particularly for identified genetic and health information transferred without a recognition or existing safeguards.","why_not_a_confirmation":"The A1 list findings only rule out the two specified A1-listed activities; they do not decide the general Article 12(1) threshold. A later confirmation of the A1 list would therefore not close this gap."},{"requirement_ref":"region_a:security_measures","gap":"Apart from encryption in transit, the facts do not establish the risk-appropriate confidentiality, availability, or regular effectiveness-testing measures, and do not establish the portal provider's access to the information or keys. The Article 14 gate cannot be decided without that security and access information.","why_not_a_confirmation":"The encrypted upload confirms one measure only (f_8c44c6e413c5). It does not establish the other Article 14 elements or the portal/key arrangements that are material to the risk assessment."},{"requirement_ref":"region_a:processing_principles","gap":"The described retention schedules do not state the actual retention periods or establish why those periods are necessary for the care purposes (f_1d30f2f75c58, f_a7a94423ed89). The facts also do not establish all security measures required to assess the principles as a whole.","why_not_a_confirmation":"The existence of care retention schedules confirms an intended retention arrangement, but not that the periods are no longer than necessary or that the associated security measures satisfy the principles."}],"notes":["Region B Health Records Act gates for permitted disclosure, service-agent agreement, minimum necessary handling, security, breach notification, data-host retention and individual access are not applicable on the supplied facts; neither clinic is a covered provider, service agent or data host under the cited definitions.","The A1 consent route for third-party disclosure remains usable for A1 professional secrecy, but it cannot be reused as the Article 19(1)(a) outward-transfer route for the genetic information.","The recognition route, the Article 19(1)(a) consent route and the clinic-contract outward-transfer route are not selected. Their failure does not create an additional blocker because the Article 18 route is available in principle.","Before proceeding, the parties must execute the approved clauses; complete the Article 18 assessment; identify the portal operator and access/key arrangements; adopt supplementary measures where necessary; and do not transfer if effective measures cannot be adopted.","Kestrel must also provide or document the Article 11 notice, create or update the Article 13 processing record, determine the Article 12(1) high-risk question, and ensure necessary retention and Article 14 security measures."]}
